## Additional invariants (Work Order 2026-08 correctness repair)

### R-A. Explicit intent declarations override lexical triggers

`intentClassifier.ts` must run an explicit-declaration pre-pass
BEFORE the lexical layer and before the LLM call.

Patterns such as `Primary research intent: opportunity_discovery`,
`Intent: feasibility`, `Use opportunity discovery`, `Treat this as a
literature review`, and `I want a recommendation report` MUST resolve
immediately to the declared intent with confidence ≥ 0.95.

An explicit declaration cannot be overridden by incidental vocabulary
such as "compare" or "recommend" appearing elsewhere in the prompt.

### R-B. Required fields are contract-derived, not globally hard-coded

`researchOrchestrator.ts` must NOT check opportunity deliverables
against a universal mega-schema (narrative briefing, build prompt,
test prompt, deployment prompt, MVP scope, etc.) unless those fields
were explicitly requested by the user or inferred and confirmed in
the plan.

Adaptive required-field validation uses:
1. `RequestedArtifact.explicitRequiredFields` — what the user stated
2. `RequestedArtifact.inferredRequiredFields` — what the plan inferred
3. Minimal universal core (title + description/rationale)

### R-C. Preamble routing must follow adjudicativeness

Non-adjudicative runs must use `withStandardPreamble(...)` for planner,
retriever, reasoner, synthesizer, verifier, and report-generation roles.
Adjudicative / PolicyOne runs must preserve the reasoning-first
`withPreamble(...)` versions of those same prompts.

`getSystemPrompt(role, isAdjudicative)` (and helpers layered on top of
it, such as `buildReasonerSystemPrompt`) is the routing boundary. Do
not call the adjudicative prompt set directly from generic
non-adjudicative paths, and do not short-circuit adjudicative runs onto
the neutral prompt set.

### R-D. Coherence Refiner is contract-bound

The Coherence Refiner prompt must include an explicit prohibition:
for non-adjudicative intents it MUST NOT add Falsification Criteria,
Contradiction Analysis, Hypothesis Testing, or adversarial sections.
Any such sections appearing in the input draft must be removed.

### R-E. Contract Auditor detects report-type bleed

The contract_auditor prompt must check for:
- Primary intent mismatch (confirmed intent ≠ report structure)
- Unauthorized falsification/adversarial sections in non-adjudicative reports
- Ranking refusal when uncertainty should instead be labeled
- Speech-act drift (opportunity list → investigation/critique)

### R-F. EZ Mode exposes output preferences

`ResearchEasyPage.tsx` must include an optional, collapsed
`Output preferences` section (toggled by a chevron button) exposing:
- Report format (default: Automatic)
- Report length (default: Standard; user can override)
- Custom word count (when Custom selected)

Explicit user selections must be sent via `requestedFormats` and
`targetWordCount` in the `startResearch` payload. They must survive
plan confirmation and reach report generation.

### R-G. Declaration tokens are normalized before alias lookup

R-A is defeated in practice if the captured declaration token is not
normalized. Users write markdown, and the capture group includes it.

`resolveIntentAlias()` MUST normalize before lookup by stripping:
surrounding whitespace; markdown emphasis (`**`, `__`, `*`, `_` wrapping
the whole token); backticks; straight and curly quotes; and trailing
punctuation. Interior underscores MUST be preserved so
`opportunity_discovery` survives.

Verified failure (commit `5ebc1d7`, PR #198 merged):

```text
"**opportunity_discovery**"    => null   ← declaration silently dropped
"opportunity_discovery"        => opportunity_discovery
```

The dropped declaration fell through to the lexical layer, which selected
`comparative` because the prompt contained the word "comparison" many
times. A single missing `.replace()` inverted a 26-minute run.

Any change to declaration capture or alias resolution must be covered by a
test matrix over: bare, `**bold**`, `*italic*`, `__underscored__`,
`` `code` ``, `"quoted"`, `'quoted'`, trailing-period, and value-on-the-
next-line forms. Secondary intent declarations must be captured too — not
only the primary.

### R-H. The verifier has no universal epistemic block

`buildVerifierPromptForIntent()` MUST NOT append evidence-tier-tag,
falsification, or contradiction-analysis requirements to every intent.
Those belong in the `verifierRubric` of the intents that warrant them
(`adjudication`, `investigation`, `story_verification`, `factual_report`,
`literature_review`, `survey`, `timeline`) — not in a shared footer.

A shared footer that mandates `(established_fact)` tags on a market
report is what makes the synthesizer emit adjudicative vocabulary in a
non-adjudicative deliverable. Scrubbing that vocabulary from display
surfaces while the verifier still demands it at generation time does not
work.

The only permitted universal minimum is speech-act neutral: no fabricated
specifics; unknown values labeled unknown; nontrivial external facts carry
a source reference; stated user constraints respected; **and the requested
deliverable is actually produced**.

`isAdjudicative` must not default to `true` on prompt-building helpers.
An omitted argument must not silently select the adjudicative prompt set.

### R-I. Refusal to deliver is a verifier FAIL

For every non-adjudicative intent, the rubric MUST treat "refused to
produce the deliverable because evidence was imperfect" as FAIL.
Uncertainty is labeled, not used to abort.

`intent_opportunity_discovery` already carries this clause. Every other
non-adjudicative intent needs it. In the reference incident the
`comparative` rubric passed a refusal essay on 6 of 8 criteria.

### R-J. Evidence insufficiency routes to discovery, never to repair

When specialists report zero or near-zero usable data, the pipeline MUST
NOT proceed to synthesis, and MUST NOT enter the bounded repair loop.
Repair without new information cannot fix data absence — it rewrites prose
and fails identically. Route back to discovery with queries reformulated
from the specific gaps the specialists named.

When discovery rounds are exhausted and the intent is non-adjudicative,
deliver the requested artifact under an explicit low-evidence labeled mode.
An essay explaining why the deliverable is impossible is not a deliverable.

### R-K. Report title and body hygiene

The report `H1` MUST be a generated title, never a truncated raw query.
The user's prompt MUST NOT be prepended to the report body — it belongs in
run metadata and the dossier Request tab.


