      the markdown/quote/punctuation normalization test matrix passes, and
      that each case fails without your fix (Rule 16).
- [ ] Did you touch `buildVerifierPromptForIntent()`? Confirm there is no
      universal epistemic footer, and that `isAdjudicative` does not
      default to `true`.
- [ ] Do the built verifier prompts for non-adjudicative intents contain no
      `established_fact` / `falsification` / `contradiction analysis`
      language — verified by test?
- [ ] Do adjudicative intents still contain them — verified by snapshot so
      PolicyOne cannot be silently weakened?
- [ ] Does every non-adjudicative rubric treat refusal-to-deliver as FAIL?
- [ ] Does evidence insufficiency route to re-discovery rather than the
      bounded repair loop?
- [ ] Is the report `H1` a generated title rather than a truncated query,
      and is the raw prompt absent from the report body?
